From: Asius <peeter@asius.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: match pending command completions

An iPhone can request its saved LTK before remote features arrive. The LTK
reply completion currently wakes the remote-features waiter. Its completion
callback drops the only connection reference while the link is BT_CONFIG.
The host disconnects immediately, and BlueZ retains a stale connected peer.

Only complete the matching request opcode. Preserve waits for later events,
including successful Command Complete events. Command credits still advance.

The later-event wait follows Chengfeng Ye's upstream proposal:
https://lore.kernel.org/linux-bluetooth/20260821164512.2842464-1-nicoyip.dev@gmail.com/
This scoped backport also checks the opcode for interleaved LTK replies.

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_event.c
@@ -4298,13 +4298,21 @@
 
 	handle_cmd_cnt_and_timer(hdev, ev->ncmd);
 
-	hci_req_cmd_complete(hdev, *opcode, *status, req_complete,
-			     req_complete_skb);
-
-	if (hci_dev_test_flag(hdev, HCI_CMD_PENDING)) {
-		bt_dev_err(hdev,
-			   "unexpected event for opcode 0x%4.4x", *opcode);
-		return;
+	/* An asynchronous reply, such as LE LTK Reply, must not complete a
+	 * different command-sync request waiting for remote features. Keep
+	 * successful commands pending when their caller requested a later event.
+	 */
+	if (!hdev->req_skb ||
+	    (hci_skb_opcode(hdev->req_skb) == *opcode &&
+	     (*status || !hci_skb_event(hdev->req_skb)))) {
+		hci_req_cmd_complete(hdev, *opcode, *status, req_complete,
+				     req_complete_skb);
+
+		if (hci_dev_test_flag(hdev, HCI_CMD_PENDING)) {
+			bt_dev_err(hdev,
+				   "unexpected event for opcode 0x%4.4x", *opcode);
+			return;
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (atomic_read(&hdev->cmd_cnt) && !skb_queue_empty(&hdev->cmd_q))
